Z||000008||BlackGT||02-01-2000||10:52 AM||||Hey Spike,<BR> When you finish the boxes I`ll be the first<BR>to buy a pair of 10" as long as they fit behind the seats....I like to feel the thump<BR>behind me hitting hard in my back! Kind of like having a pair of vibrating seats for those long cruises. I`m shopping for a new<BR>CD head unit and amp for the subs along<BR>with new speakers for up front. When it`s<BR>finished I want to be able to enjoy whatever<BR>I`m in the mood to listen too but not let<BR>the whole neighborhood(THIEVES!) know that<BR>there is a killer system in the car! Keep <BR>us posted!!<BR> ||||reg||6
Z||000009||spike||02-01-2000||01:30 PM||||Sorry I do not have any pictures, the silicone is used on the inside of the box just to make sure it is air tight. I use wood glue and screws to join the wood. This custom box cannot hold 1 sub, must be 2. I also had made 2 small ports to give the subs more breathing room. The box is a little small for a pair of subs. The weired thing is that it sounds better with the ports blocked-off. With this system you are able to see the box from outside the car. It is not hidden so a alarm is a must. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||spike||02-01-2000||01:42 PM||||It is quite hard to build the box because each piece of wood requirs a midor cut (angled). My first box took about 2 days to get it perfect. I am sure the second one will also take some time to build. Once I have one made the rest shoul be a piece of cake (I hope). I heard someone was selling a box to fit in the front compartment for about 200.00 (cdn or us dollars, not sure). Anyone think of a fair price yet. I wish I had a picture of the box to show you people. I am sure that you would love the way it looks. I had many good comments about my custom made sub box.||||reg||1
